	(text "Two pull resistors per LA channel, both on the J1 side of the LSF0108 (An_B): a 10k and a 2.2k, both from the same expander:\nU54 (0x21, ADDR = VCCP) for LA1-LA7 and LA9, U18 (0x20, ADDR = GND) for LA8 and LA10-LA14.\nWhich expander pin serves which channel follows the PCB layout (U54 at 90 deg, U18 at 270 deg), so the traces do not cross; firmware takes the map from this netlist.\nEach port: high = pull-up to VREF_OUT, low = pull-down to GND, input = off. Per channel: 10k, 2.2k or both (about 1.8k),\nup or down. Firmware picks the strength from the pin function (I2C 2.2k, UART RX 10k, 5 V SPI outputs 2.2k).\nKeep both ports of a channel in the same direction (opposite = a divider that draws current).\nVREF_OUT follows LA_VCCIO (1.8 / 3.3 V) or 5 V, so the pulls follow the I/O voltage; in 5 V mode a pull-up lifts a pod-driven high to 5 V.\nPULL_RST (PG7) low = both expanders in reset, all ports inputs, pulls off. R64 holds it low while the STM32 boots;\nfirmware turns VREF_OUT on first, then releases PULL_RST (TI: ramp VCCP before VCCI, else SDA can stick low).\nOld firmware (TCA9554 driver at 0x20) only reaches U18 output/input registers, never its direction registers: pulls stay off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1fd8999f-6349-47f6-a56e-deb6eb5699bb")
	)
	(text "U54 TCA6416A, 0x21: LA1-LA7, LA9"
